Fri Nov 13 17:30:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- polkit rule: every YES now checks the remote (origin) or that the ref
  is not a runtime. Flatpak's policy implies runtime-install from
  app-update and runtime-uninstall from app-uninstall, so the unconditional
  YES let vilna-apps install runtimes from any remote and remove runtimes.
- search and describe no longer carry openWorldHint, which made Herkos
  ask before every search.
- Remove the empty mount points Flatpak leaves in its system cache.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 14:00:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- Initial package: MCP servers "programs" (vilna-mcp-apps: search,
  describe, list, install, update, remove Flatpak apps from Flathub and
  Vilna) and "launcher" (vilna-mcp-launcher: open an installed app),
  ADR 0012. Started only by Herkos; the system user vilna-apps and its
  polkit rule (install, update and remove only, no new sources).
